MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The 1/4-20 machine screws felt like plausible companions to my UNC rivet nuts because matching threads could let me use supplies I already have, provided the length fits.",
    "The lag-bolt assortment and complete screw, nut, and washer sets fit my recent habit of gathering practical fastening supplies: varied lengths support different assemblies, and matching components save me from finding each piece separately."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The pipe nipples and pressure gauge need a piping or pressure-system project that my recent purchases do not indicate. Owning other measuring tools does not give me a reason to measure pressure.",
    "The self-tapping screws serve a different fastening purpose from bolts that mate with threaded inserts. The trash cans and printing-pen filament also lack a clear connection to an immediate need or equipment I have indicated owning."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Stainless steel and familiar screw dimensions seemed to count too heavily; material and size alone do not establish that a fastener works with my existing parts.",
    "My interest in DIY tools and occasional craft supplies seemed to stretch into unrelated workshop supplies and printing-pen consumables without a specific use connecting them."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Thread standard, pitch, length, and fastening method matter together. A familiar diameter is only a starting point when I need parts that actually mate.",
    "I often buy assortments that prepare me for several jobs. Fifty identical long M5 bolts or a pack of one lock-nut size can fit my interests while still being something I would postpone until a particular assembly needs them."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my fastening and fabrication interests, but sometimes treated broad workshop similarity as enough without a compatible part or current project need."
}
